Based on the symptom—SMS‐mode button “1”/“2” coming out on MD‐core A/B instead of B/C—the change almost certainly needs to happen wherever MD vs. SMS mode is detected and the raw USB/SNAC controller bits are remapped. That logically lives in two FPGA modules (the top-level that switches mapping and the lower-level that actually wires MD‐pad lines to SMS pad lines) and in the SNAC interface on the CPU side that hands off the USB buttons.

The four files most likely in need of adjustment are thus:

1. The SNAC interface source where the USB controller buttons get turned into raw MD signals:  
   `software/snac_interface.c`

2. The top-level MD FPGA file that detects SMS mode and selects one of two button-mappers:  
   `fpga/megadrive/megadrive_core.vhd`

3. The MD-to-SMS button mapper that currently drives SMS “TL”/“TR” (B/C) out onto MD “A”/“B”:  
   `fpga/megadrive/controller_mapper.vhd`

4. The lower-level joypad I/O wrapper that actually assigns pad pins to the final output bits:  
   `fpga/megadrive/joypad_input.vhd`

```  
software/snac_interface.c  
fpga/megadrive/megadrive_core.vhd  
fpga/megadrive/controller_mapper.vhd  
fpga/megadrive/joypad_input.vhd  
```
