I focussed on the VCO core itself (vco.sv) where the clock-domain crossing and memory-read timing almost certainly need adjustment for iCE40’s LUT-RAM, the example top that instantiates it (so its clocking must match the new 48 kHz structure), and the two python LUT generators which still use the old rate (46875 Hz) and thus will produce the wrong step values under the new clocking.

