│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                       1. What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The testbench in testing/bsg_test/bsg_nonsynth_dpi/top.v           │
│ instantiates two clock generators that both drive the same net     │
│ ns_clk.                                                            │
│                                                                    │
│ That means ns_clk is being multiply driven, which is               │
│ invalid/unsafe for a clock signal and can lead to simulation       │
│ ambiguity or incorrect behavior. The issue description suggests    │
│ this is related to black-parrot issue #798, where multiple clock   │
│ generators in the testbench are causing problems.                  │
│                                                                    │
│                    2. Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The problem is in testing/bsg_test/bsg_nonsynth_dpi/top.v,         │
│ specifically these two instances:                                  │
│                                                                    │
│  • core_clk_gen (.o(ns_clk));                                      │
│  • core_clk_gen2 (.o(ns_clk));                                     │
│                                                                    │
│ Both are connected to the same output net ns_clk.                  │
│                                                                    │
│               3. Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • A single clock net should have exactly one driver unless there  │
│    is a deliberate resolved-net design.                            │
│  • If a second clock source is needed, it should drive a different │
│    signal.                                                         │
│  • Testbenches should avoid multiply driving clocks because that   │
│    can create nondeterministic simulation results.                 │
│  • If the second clock generator is unnecessary, remove it rather  │
│    than leaving dead or conflicting logic.                         │
│                                                                    │
│                     4. How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ The minimal and correct fix is to remove the second clock          │
│ generator instance (core_clk_gen2) so that ns_clk is driven by     │
│ only one source.                                                   │
│                                                                    │
