│                                                                    │
│ The module bsg_mem_1rw_sync_mask_write_bit_from_1r1w.sv references │
│ addr_li before it is declared.                                     │
│ Although some HDL tools allow this, others like Questa/Modelsim    │
│ and Synopsys DC reject it because the signal is used in an         │
│ expression before its declaration appears in the source.           │
│                                                                    │
│                    2. Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ In:                                                                │
│                                                                    │
│ bsg_mem/bsg_mem_1rw_sync_mask_write_bit_from_1r1w.sv               │
│                                                                    │
│ the code currently does this:                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • addr_match uses addr_li                                         │
│  • addr_li is declared only afterward                              │
│                                                                    │
│ So the problematic sequence is:                                    │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  wire                      addr_match = w_addr_r == addr_li;       │
│  wire                      bypass_n = v_and_w_r & addr_match;      │
│  wire                      bypass_r;                               │
│                                                                    │
│  wire [addr_width_lp-1:0]  addr_li = els_p > 1 ? addr_i : '0;      │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│               3. Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Declare signals before they are referenced in continuous        │
│    assignments or expressions.                                     │
│  • Prefer source order that is compatible with stricter HDL        │
│    compilers.                                                      │
│  • Make minimal changes that preserve behavior.                    │
│  • Avoid unnecessary refactoring when a simple reorder fixes the   │
│    issue.                                                          │
│                                                                    │
│                          4. How to fix it                          │
│                                                                    │
│ Move the declaration of addr_li above its first use, so that       │
│ addr_match is assigned only after addr_li has already been         │
│ declared.                                                          │
