│                                                                    │
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                       1) What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The lockstep checker is missing a class of faults on core_busy_o   │
│ from the non-lockstep core.                                        │
│                                                                    │
│ The root cause is that the non-lockstep core and the lockstep core │
│ share the same gated clock (clk). Since core_busy_q controls clock │
│ gating, a transient low glitch on core_busy_o can gate off the     │
│ lockstep core in the same cycle that the regular core’s            │
│ core_busy_o is being observed. As a result, the lockstep core      │
│ never samples the faulty value, so the mismatch is not detected    │
│ and no major alert is raised.                                      │
│                                                                    │
│                    2) Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is in rtl/ibex_top.sv around the shared clock gating:    │
│                                                                    │
│  • core_busy_q is used to derive clock_en                          │
│  • clock_en gates the single core clock clk                        │
│  • that same clk is used by both:                                  │
│     • u_ibex_core                                                  │
│     • u_ibex_lockstep                                              │
│                                                                    │
│ Relevant locations:                                                │
│                                                                    │
│  • assign clock_en = core_busy_q | debug_req_i | irq_pending |     │
│    irq_nm_i;                                                       │
│  • prim_clock_gating ... .clk_o(clk)                               │
│  • u_ibex_core(.clk_i(clk), ...)                                   │
│  • u_ibex_lockstep(.clk_i(clk), ...)                               │
│                                                                    │
│ The comparison logic in rtl/ibex_lockstep.sv is fine in principle; │
│ the issue is that the checker can be clock-gated away before it    │
│ can observe the mismatch.                                          │
│                                                                    │
│               3) Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep the fix minimal and localized.                             │
│  • Preserve existing functional behavior for normal operation.     │
│  • Ensure the lockstep checker remains able to sample and compare  │
│    the non-lockstep core output when that output is used for clock │
│    gating.                                                         │
│  • Avoid broad architectural changes unless necessary.             │
