│                                                                    │
│                       1. What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The lockstep checker is intended to detect mismatches between the  │
│ main Ibex core and the shadow/lockstep core. However, the main     │
│ core’s core_busy_o signal is also used to generate the clock       │
│ enable (clock_en) for both cores.                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ Because the lockstep core is clock-gated using the same clock_en   │
│ derived from the non-lockstep core, a short low glitch on          │
│ core_busy_o can gate off the lockstep core before it samples the   │
│ mismatched value. That prevents the comparison logic from seeing   │
│ the mismatch and from raising a major alert.                       │
│                                                                    │
│                    2. Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The relevant logic is in rtl/ibex_top.sv:                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • core_busy_q contributes to clock_en                             │
│  • clock_en drives prim_clock_gating                               │
│  • the gated clock clk is used for both:                           │
│     • u_ibex_core                                                  │
│     • u_ibex_lockstep                                              │
│                                                                    │
│ So the clock gating is shared, and the lockstep core can be        │
│ disabled too early relative to the main core’s transient glitch.   │
│                                                                    │
│ The comparison logic itself is in rtl/ibex_lockstep.sv:            │
│                                                                    │
│  • outputs_mismatch = enable_cmp_q & (shadow_outputs_q !=          │
│    core_outputs_q[0]);                                             │
│                                                                    │
│ This logic is correct, but it only works if both sides remain      │
│ clocked long enough for the mismatch to be captured.               │
│                                                                    │
│               3. Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
