│                                                                    │
│                        1. Problem statement                        │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is an out-of-bounds array access in the data-side access │
│ tracking logic in ibex_top.sv.                                     │
│                                                                    │
│ In the always_comb block that updates pending_dside_accesses_d[i], │
│ the code evaluates:                                                │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  pending_dside_accesses_shifted[i - 1].valid                       │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ when i == 0 is possible. That means the design can attempt to read │
│ index -1, which is invalid and can cause simulation/synthesis      │
│ issues or undefined behavior.                                      │
│                                                                    │
│                    2. Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The problematic code is in:                                        │
│                                                                    │
│  • rtl/ibex_top.sv                                                 │
│  • inside the for (genvar i = 0; i < MaxOutstandingDSideAccesses;  │
│    i++) begin : g_dside_tracker                                    │
│  • specifically in the always_comb block around the request-grant  │
│    logic:                                                          │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  if (data_req_o && data_gnt_i) begin                               │
│    if (i == 0 && !pending_dside_accesses_shifted[i].valid) begin   │
│      ...                                                           │
│    end else if (pending_dside_accesses_shifted[i - 1].valid &      │
│                 !pending_dside_accesses_shifted[i].valid) begin    │
│      ...                                                           │
│    end                                                             │
│  end                                                               │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Even though the i == 0 case is handled first, the structure relies │
│ on conditional evaluation behavior in a way that is fragile and    │
│ still flagged as an out-of-bounds risk. The fix should explicitly  │
│ separate the i == 0 case from all other cases.                     │
│                                                                    │
│                    3. Best practices to follow                     │
│                                                                    │
│  • Avoid any expression that can index arrays with negative        │
│    values, even if guarded by a condition.                         │
│  • Explicitly separate boundary cases (i == 0) from general cases  │
│    (i > 0).                                                        │
│  • Keep the change minimal and localized to the affected logic.    │
│  • Preserve the existing behavior for all valid indices.           │
│  • Prefer clear, structurally safe control flow over relying on    │
│    short-circuiting or nested conditions.                          │
│                                                                    │
│                          4. How to fix it                          │
│                                                                    │
│ Refactor the always_comb block so that:                            │
│                                                                    │
│  • when i == 0, only the i == 0 logic is evaluated;                │
│  • for i > 0, the logic using i - 1 is evaluated only in that      │
│    branch.                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│ A clean way is to wrap the request-grant update logic in:          │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  if (i == 0) begin                                                 │
│    ...                                                             │
│  end else begin                                                    │
│    ...                                                             │
│  end                                                               │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This guarantees i - 1 is never evaluated when i == 0.              │
