│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                       1. What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is an out-of-bounds array access in the dside            │
│ pending-access tracking logic.                                     │
│ In the always_comb block, the code uses                            │
│ pending_dside_accesses_shifted[i - 1] when deciding whether to     │
│ insert a new pending access. If i == 0, this becomes               │
│ pending_dside_accesses_shifted[-1], which is invalid and can lead  │
│ to undefined behavior or synthesis/simulation errors.              │
│                                                                    │
│                    2. Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The problematic code is in rtl/ibex_top.sv inside the              │
│ g_dside_tracker generate loop, specifically this condition:        │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  else if (pending_dside_accesses_shifted[i - 1].valid &            │
│           !pending_dside_accesses_shifted[i].valid) begin          │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This is reached in the always_comb block that computes             │
│ pending_dside_accesses_d[i].                                       │
│                                                                    │
│               3. Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Avoid index arithmetic that can produce invalid indices,        │
│    especially in hardware description languages where              │
│    out-of-bounds behavior is unsafe.                               │
│  • Handle boundary conditions explicitly, particularly for i == 0. │
│  • Keep the fix minimal and local to avoid changing intended       │
│    functionality.                                                  │
│  • Preserve the existing access-tracking semantics for all valid   │
│    entries.                                                        │
│                                                                    │
│                     4. How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Refactor the conditional logic so that the i == 0 case is handled  │
│ separately from the i > 0 case.                                    │
│ For i == 0, only allow insertion into slot 0 when it is empty.     │
│ For i > 0, keep the existing dependency on the previous slot, but  │
│ only reference i - 1 when it is guaranteed to be valid.            │
