│                                                                    │
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                       1) What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The OTBN coverage collectors are defining mnemonic coverpoint bins │
│ using stringized identifiers like "mnem_addi" instead of the       │
│ actual mnemonic values like "addi" or addi-typed string literals.  │
│                                                                    │
│ After commit e9986ef486, the DEF_MNEM_BIN macro was changed to add │
│ quotes around the macro argument to satisfy Verissimo. That made   │
│ the coverpoint bins expect string values that include the extra    │
│ quoting behavior, while the sampling code still passes the plain   │
│ mnemonic text. As a result, valid mnemonics are not matched by any │
│ bin and get counted as illegal_bins, causing coverage collection   │
│ to fail the tests.                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│                    2) Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is in:                                                   │
│                                                                    │
│  • hw/ip/otbn/dv/uvm/env/otbn_env_cov.sv                           │
│     • DEF_MNEM_BIN macro definition                                │
│     • covergroups such as:                                         │
│        • enc_ecall_cg                                              │
│        • enc_i_cg                                                  │
│        • pairwise_insn_cg                                          │
│        • other mnemonic-based covergroups that use mnem_str_t      │
│          sampling and DEF_MNEM_BIN(...)                            │
│                                                                    │
│ The specific mismatch is between:                                  │
│                                                                    │
│  • bin values created by DEF_MNEM_BIN                              │
│  • sampled mnemonic values passed into covergroup sample(...)      │
│                                                                    │
│               3) Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Make the fix minimal and localized.                             │
│  • Preserve the intent of the Verissimo workaround if possible,    │
│    but do not let it change the functional meaning of coverpoint   │
│    bins.                                                           │
│  • Keep the covergroup bins aligned with the actual type/value     │
│    produced by the sampler.                                        │
│  • Avoid broad refactors unless strictly necessary.                │
│  • Prefer a fix that restores correct coverage semantics while     │
│    maintaining compatibility with lint/syntax requirements.        │
│                                                                    │
│                     4) How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ The best fix is to adjust the mnemonic bin macro so it creates     │
│ bins that match the actual mnemonic string values used at sampling │
│ time, rather than quoted macro names.                              │
│                                                                    │
│ In practice, this means:                                           │
│                                                                    │
│  • DEF_MNEM_BIN(NAME) should expand to a bin containing the string │
│    value corresponding to the mnemonic itself, not the macro       │
│    identifier as a quoted token.                                   │
│  • If Verissimo requires quoting for syntactic reasons, then the   │
│    quoting must be done in a way that still yields the actual      │
│    runtime string value, not "mnem_addi"-style literal names.      │
│                                                                    │
│ Given the issue report and the observed failure, the simplest and  │
│ correct fix is to restore the pre-change behavior for mnemonic bin │
│ contents so coverage sampling matches valid mnemonic values again. │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│                    Phase 2: FIX IMPLEMENTATION                     │
│                                                                    │
│                           modification 1                           │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  [file]hw/ip/otbn/dv/uvm/env/otbn_env_cov.sv[/file]                │
│  [original]                                                        │
│  `define DEF_MNEM_BIN(NAME) bins NAME = {`"NAME`"}                 │
│  [/original]                                                       │
│  [patched]                                                         │
