│                       1) What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The OTBN DV coverage code changed the way mnemonic covergroup bins │
│ are defined.                                                       │
│ After commit e9986ef486, the macro defining mnemonic bins now      │
│ inserts quotes around the bin name, so a bin like:                 │
│                                                                    │
│  • mnem_addi                                                       │
│                                                                    │
│ is effectively being matched against a string literal form like:   │
│                                                                    │
│  • "mnem_addi"                                                     │
│                                                                    │
│ But the covergroup sample functions are still called with the      │
│ mnemonic value itself, e.g. addi or bn.add, not the quoted string  │
│ "addi".                                                            │
│                                                                    │
│ As a result, coverage sampling treats valid mnemonics as unmatched │
│ values, which triggers illegal_bins other = default; and causes    │
│ coverage-enabled simulations to fail.                              │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                    2) Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
