│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  `define DEF_MNEM_BIN(NAME) bins NAME = {`"NAME`"}                 │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This macro expands to a quoted string based on the macro name, not │
│ the actual mnemonic string value used by the sample function.      │
│                                                                    │
│ This affects coverpoints such as:                                  │
│                                                                    │
│  • enc_i_cg.mnemonic_cp                                            │
│  • pairwise_insn_cg.last_cp                                        │
│  • pairwise_insn_cg.cur_cp                                         │
│  • other mnemonic coverpoints using DEF_MNEM_BIN                   │
│                                                                    │
│ The sample functions elsewhere in the environment pass mnemonic    │
│ strings like addi rather than "mnem_addi".                         │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│               3) Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep coverage bin values aligned with sampled values:           │
│    coverpoints must compare the same representation that is passed │
│    to sample().                                                    │
│  • Make the fix minimal: avoid changing the sampling pipeline if   │
│    only the bin definitions are wrong.                             │
│  • Preserve Verissimo compatibility: if quotes were added to       │
│    satisfy a tool requirement, keep the representation that the    │
│    tool expects, but ensure it still matches sampled values.       │
│  • Prefer fixing the macro at the source rather than changing      │
│    every call site or every sample function.                       │
│                                                                    │
