│    runtime sampling path, unless the latter is required by tool    │
│    constraints.                                                    │
│  • Avoid touching unrelated environment code (otbn_env.sv) unless  │
│    there is evidence it affects the mnemonic encoding.             │
│                                                                    │
│                     4. How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ The cleanest fix is to adjust the mnemonic bin macro so the        │
│ coverpoint bins match the actual string values being sampled.      │
│                                                                    │
│ Concretely, the macro should define bins using the mnemonic string │
│ value rather than the quoted macro name token. If Verissimo        │
│ requires quoted strings in source, then the sampled/defined type   │
│ should be aligned accordingly; however, from the issue description │
│ and the code shown, the real mismatch is that the bins are         │
│ expecting the wrong textual form. The fix should therefore make    │
│ the mnemonic bins correspond to the unquoted mnemonic values that  │
│ are passed to sample().                                            │
│                                                                    │
│ If Verissimo truly requires the quoted form in this location, then │
│ the alternative would be to ensure the sampled values are          │
│ generated with quotes too, but that would be more invasive and is  │
│ not necessary if the coverpoint bins can directly use the string   │
│ literals already stored in the mnemonic variables.                 │
