│  er-25k.html), [Tang Nano                                          │
│  20K](https://wiki.sipeed.com/hardware/en/tang/tang-nano-20k/nano  │
│  0k.html) and [Tang Primer                                         │
│  20K](https://wiki.sipeed.com/hardware/en/tang/tang-primer-20k/pr  │
│  er-20k.html).                                                     │
│  +                                                                 │
│  +Main features,                                                   │
│  +                                                                 │
│  +- 720p HDMI output with sound.                                   │
│  +- Cycle accurate gameplay quality has been achieved since the N  │
│  circuits have been almost entirely replicated.                    │
│  +- Rom loading from MicroSD cards with an easy-to-use menu syste  │
│  +- Playstation 2 controllers support and experimental USB gamepa  │
│  support.                                                          │
│  +                                                                 │
│  +## Pick a Board                                                  │
│  +                                                                 │
│  +You need either the Sipeed Tang Primer 25K or Tang Nano 20K FPG  │
│  board to run the latest NESTang.                                  │
│  +                                                                 │
│  +* The Tang Primer 25K is the latest small-form-factor, modular   │
│  FPGA board from Sipeed. If you want more memory and extensibilit  │
│  choose Primer 25K. You need to get the [main Primer 25K dock      │
│  board](https://wiki.sipeed.com/hardware/en/tang/tang-primer-25k/  │
│  imer-25k.html), [DVI                                              │
│  PMod](https://wiki.sipeed.com/hardware/en/tang/tang-PMOD/FPGA_PM  │
│  .html#PMOD_DVI), [TF Card                                         │
│  PMod](https://wiki.sipeed.com/hardware/en/tang/tang-PMOD/FPGA_PM  │
│  .html#PMOD_TF-CARD), [DS2x2                                       │
│  PMod](https://wiki.sipeed.com/hardware/en/tang/tang-PMOD/FPGA_PM  │
│  .html#PMOD_DS2x2) and a [Tang                                     │
│  SDRAM](https://wiki.sipeed.com/hardware/en/tang/tang-PMOD/FPGA_P  │
│  D.html#TANG-40P-MODULE).                                          │
│  +* The Tang Nano 20K is a tiny and popular FPGA dongle. The boar  │
│  also features 8MB of FPGA-gaming-friendly SDRAM memory. Be sure   │
│  get the [Tang Nano 20K Retro Gaming                               │
│  Kit](https://www.amazon.com/GW2AR-18-Computer-Debugger-Multiple-  │
│  ulator/dp/B0C5XLBQ6C), as it contains the necessary controllers   │
│  and adapters.                                                     │
│  +                                                                 │
│  +## Installation                                                  │
│  +                                                                 │
│  +A [step-by-step                                                  │
│  instructions](https://github.com/nand2mario/snestang/blob/main/d  │
│  /installation.md) is available for installation. Here are quick   │
│  instructions for the more experienced,                            │
│  +                                                                 │
│  +* Tang Primer 25K needs 4 modules: Tang sdram, DVI, Dualshock2,  │
│  SD and a pair of dualshock controllers. Currently these should    │
│  cost ~$60 in total. Tang Nano 20K just needs controller adapters  │
│  Check                                                             │
│  [instructions](https://github.com/nand2mario/snestang/blob/main/  │
│  c/installation.md) for how to connect the modules / adapters.     │
│  +* Download a NESTang release from                                │
│  [github](https://github.com/nand2mario/nestang/releases). The     │
│  bitstream (`nestang_*.fs`) should be written to flash at address  │
│  0. The firmware (`firmware.bin`) should be written to 0x500000    │
│  (5MB).                                                            │
│  +* A MicroSD card to hold ROMs.                                   │
│  +* Connect one or two DualShock2 controllers to the DS2 pmod. Or  │
│  you can connect one USB gamepad to use the [experimental USB      │
│  gamepad support](doc/usb_gamepad.md). The board only has one USB  │
│  port. So use DS2 if you want two players.                         │
│  +                                                                 │
│  +* NES controller wiring: connect the NES controller's DATA,      │
│  LATCH, and CLOCK pins to the controller adapter / FPGA GPIO pins  │
│  used by the NES controller interface. Use a 3.3V-compatible leve  │
│  shifter or a proper resistor/logic level converter if your        │
│  controller is powered from 5V.                                    │
│  +* Insert the MicroSD card, connect an HDMI monitor or TV, and    │
│  enjoy your games.                                                 │
│  +                                                                 │
│  +Version 0.4 also supports [tang primer 20k](doc/primer20k.md).   │
│  +                                                                 │
│  +## Development                                                   │
│  +                                                                 │
│  +If you want to generate the bitstream from source, see [Build    │
│  Instructions](https://nand2mario.github.io/nestang-doc/dev/build  │
│  itstream/). The recommended Gowin IDE version is 1.9.9 commercia  │
│  (requires a free license).                                        │
│  +                                                                 │
│  +[Usb_hid_host](https://github.com/nand2mario/usb_hid_host) was   │
│  development so NESTang could support USB gamepads. Follow the li  │
│  if you want to use it for your FPGA projects. It supports         │
│  keyboards and mice too.                                           │
│  +                                                                 │
│  +## Next steps                                                    │
│  +                                                                 │
│  +See NESTang [changes.md](CHANGES.md).                            │
│  +                                                                 │
│  +Here are what I may work on when I get time. No promise though.  │
│  Suggestions and pull requests are welcome!                        │
│  +* Cheats support.                                                │
│  +* Saves and loads.                                               │
│  +                                                                 │
