│                                                                    │
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                       1) What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ rvfi_mode is an RVFI output signal that is only assigned when a    │
│ valid retirement happens:                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • wb_valid_adjusted && !is_dummy_instr_wb_i                       │
│                                                                    │
│ Because of that, when the design comes out of reset, rvfi_mode is  │
│ never explicitly initialized. This leaves it with an undefined     │
│ value (X) until the first qualifying instruction retires.          │
│                                                                    │
│                    2) Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is in bhv/cv32e40s_rvfi.sv:                              │
│                                                                    │
│  • rvfi_mode is declared as an output at the module interface.     │
│  • It is reset in the always_ff reset branch for many RVFI         │
│    signals, but not for rvfi_mode.                                 │
│  • The only assignment in normal operation is here:                │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  rvfi_mode <= priv_lvl_i;                                          │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ inside:                                                            │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  if (wb_valid_adjusted && !is_dummy_instr_wb_i) begin              │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ So rvfi_mode lacks a reset value.                                  │
│                                                                    │
│               3) Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • All stateful output registers should be explicitly reset to a   │
│    known value.                                                    │
│  • Reset values should be consistent with the                      │
│    architectural/default privilege mode expected at reset.         │
│  • The fix should be minimal and not alter retirement behavior     │
│    beyond initialization.                                          │
│  • Avoid changing combinational/functional logic unless necessary. │
│                                                                    │
│                     4) How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Add rvfi_mode <= '0; in the reset branch of the always_ff block in │
│ bhv/cv32e40s_rvfi.sv, alongside the other RVFI signal resets.      │
│                                                                    │
│ This ensures rvfi_mode has a deterministic value immediately after │
│ reset.                                                             │
