│                                                                    │
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                         1. Problem summary                         │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue says that the values of MVENDORID, MARCHID, and MIMPID   │
│ are currently inherited from Ibex, but they need to be updated to  │
│ the CVE2-specific values. These are architectural CSR              │
│ identification registers, so their values should reflect the CVE2  │
│ core rather than Ibex.                                             │
│                                                                    │
│                    2. Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The relevant code is in:                                           │
│                                                                    │
│  • rtl/cve2_pkg.sv                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The problematic definitions are:                                   │
│                                                                    │
│  • CSR_MVENDORID_VALUE                                             │
│  • CSR_MARCHID_VALUE                                               │
│  • CSR_MIMPID_VALUE                                                │
│                                                                    │
│ These are currently set to Ibex-oriented values:                   │
│                                                                    │
│  • MVENDORID = 0                                                   │
│  • MARCHID = 22                                                    │
│  • MIMPID = 0                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ The CSR address enum in the same file is fine; the bug is in the   │
│ CSR value constants.                                               │
│                                                                    │
│               3. Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Use the official CVE2 values as documented by the project or    │
│    referenced manuals.                                             │
│  • Keep the fix minimal and local to the constant definitions.     │
│  • Avoid changing unrelated CSR behavior or CSR decoding logic.    │
│  • Preserve the existing coding style and parameter naming.        │
│  • Ensure the values are consistent with the RISC-V CSR            │
│    specification:                                                  │
│     • MVENDORID should identify the vendor if assigned, or remain  │
│       0 if intentionally unimplemented.                            │
│     • MARCHID should identify the architecture/core family         │
│       correctly.                                                   │
│     • MIMPID should identify the implementation version if one is  │
│       assigned, or remain 0 if intentionally unimplemented.        │
│                                                                    │
│                     4. How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Update the three localparams in rtl/cve2_pkg.sv to the             │
│ CVE2-specific values. Since the issue explicitly states they must  │
│ “match the CVE2 values” and points to the CV32E40X user manual as  │
│ an example, the correct fix is to replace the Ibex-derived         │
│ constants with the CVE2-defined ones in that package file.         │
│                                                                    │
