│                                                                    │
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                       1) What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The FMA module currently assumes that the addend operand operand_c │
│ always uses the destination/result floating-point format           │
│ (dst_fmt_i).                                                       │
│                                                                    │
│ That is fine for standard fused multiply-add operations where the  │
│ addend matches the result format. But it prevents supporting       │
│ certain widening vector FP add/sub instructions where the addend   │
│ should instead be interpreted in the source format (src_fmt_i)     │
│ when both operands are narrow and the result is wide.              │
│                                                                    │
│ So the limitation is not in the arithmetic itself, but in how      │
│ operand C is unpacked and classified.                              │
│                                                                    │
│                    2) Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is in src/fpnew_fma_multi.sv, in the operand unpacking   │
│ logic inside always_comb begin : op_select:                        │
│                                                                    │
│  • operand_c is built from fmt_*[dst_fmt_q][2]                     │
│  • info_c is taken from info_q[dst_fmt_q][2]                       │
│                                                                    │
│ These lines hardwire the addend to the destination format.         │
│                                                                    │
│ Relevant location:                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│  • src/fpnew_fma_multi.sv around the op_select block               │
│                                                                    │
