│                                                                    │
│                       1) What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The FMA implementation currently assumes that the addend operand   │
│ operand_c has the same floating-point format as the result         │
│ (dst_fmt_i).                                                       │
│                                                                    │
│ That is correct for standard fused multiply-accumulate operations, │
│ but it prevents support for some widening vector floating-point    │
│ add/sub operations where the addend is narrower than the result.   │
│ In those cases, the addend should be unpacked using src_fmt_i, not │
│ dst_fmt_i.                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│ So the issue is not that the FMA cannot mathematically handle it,  │
│ but that the operand unpacking logic hardcodes the addend format   │
│ to dst_fmt_i.                                                      │
│                                                                    │
