│                                                                    │
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                       1) What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is that fpnew_cast_multi.sv handles                      │
│ integer-to-floating-point (I2F) overflow incorrectly.              │
│                                                                    │
│ According to IEEE 754, when converting an integer to floating      │
│ point and the rounded result exceeds the destination               │
│ floating-point range, the operation should raise overflow (OF). It │
│ should not raise invalid (NV) for that case.                       │
│                                                                    │
│ In the current implementation, the code suppresses overflow for    │
│ I2F and instead sets NV, which is the opposite of the required     │
│ behavior.                                                          │
│                                                                    │
│                    2) Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The problematic logic is in:                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • src/fpnew_cast_multi.sv                                         │
│  • specifically around the regular floating-point status           │
│    generation for casts                                            │
│                                                                    │
│ The relevant code is:                                              │
│                                                                    │
│  • fp_regular_status.NV = src_is_int_q & (of_before_round |        │
│    of_after_round);                                                │
│  • fp_regular_status.OF = ~src_is_int_q & (...);                   │
│  • fp_regular_status.NX = src_is_int_q ? ... : ...                 │
│                                                                    │
│ This means that when the source is an integer, overflow is being   │
│ reported as invalid, and OF is being disabled.                     │
│                                                                    │
│               3) Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Follow IEEE 754 exception semantics:                            │
│     • I2F overflow should set OF and usually NX                    │
│     • NV should not be used for normal range overflow in I2F       │
│  • Keep the fix minimal and localized.                             │
│  • Avoid changing unrelated integer special-case handling.         │
│  • Preserve existing behavior for F2I and special-case paths       │
│    unless they are directly affected.                              │
│  • Maintain the current structure of the status assignment logic   │
│    where possible.                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│                     4) How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ The fix should be to change the regular FP status generation so    │
│ that:                                                              │
│                                                                    │
│  • OF is asserted when an integer source overflows during I2F      │
│  • NV is not asserted for that overflow condition                  │
│  • NX remains asserted when rounding/inexactness occurs, including │
│    overflow-induced rounding                                       │
│                                                                    │
│ In practice, this means updating the status assignment block so    │
│ that OF is driven for both integer and floating-point sources when │
│ appropriate, and removing the incorrect NV assignment for          │
│ integer-to-float overflow.                                         │
│                                                                    │
