│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                       1) What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is that CVFPU handles integer-to-floating-point          │
│ conversions (I2F) incorrectly when the integer value cannot be     │
│ represented exactly in the destination floating-point format.      │
│                                                                    │
│ According to IEEE 754, this situation should raise overflow (OF)   │
│ for floating-point results.                                        │
│ However, the current implementation suppresses OF for I2F and      │
│ instead sets invalid (NV), which is not correct for this case.     │
│                                                                    │
│ This behavior is especially relevant for half precision, where     │
│ some integer values may overflow the representable range. For      │
│ single and double precision, this usually cannot happen for        │
│ 32-bit/64-bit integer widths.                                      │
│                                                                    │
│                    2) Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The problematic logic is in:                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • src/fpnew_cast_multi.sv                                         │
│  • specifically in the fp_regular_status assignments around the    │
│    result selection logic                                          │
│                                                                    │
│ The key lines are:                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  assign fp_regular_status.NV = src_is_int_q & (of_before_round |   │
│  of_after_round); // overflow is invalid for I2F casts             │
│  assign fp_regular_status.OF = ~src_is_int_q & (~info_q.is_inf &   │
│  (of_before_round | of_after_round)); // inf casts no OF           │
│  assign fp_regular_status.NX = src_is_int_q ? (|                   │
│  fp_round_sticky_bits) // overflow is invalid in i2f               │
│            : (| fp_round_sticky_bits) | (~info_q.is_inf &          │
│  (of_before_round | of_after_round));                              │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
