│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                       1. What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The bug is that CVFPU incorrectly raises the IEEE-754 inexact flag │
│ (NX) when converting an infinity with F2F casts.                   │
│                                                                    │
│ Per IEEE 754, converting infinity to another floating-point format │
│ should not, by itself, signal inexact.                             │
│ However, the current implementation still computes NX from sticky  │
│ bits derived from the mantissa path, and those sticky bits become  │
│ set for infinity because the mantissa is filled with all 1s during │
│ special handling.                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│                    2. Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is in src/fpnew_cast_multi.sv:                           │
│                                                                    │
│  • Location #1: infinity handling sets:                            │
│     • final_exp                                                    │
│     • preshift_mant = '1                                           │
│     • of_before_round = 1'b1                                       │
│  • Location #2: fp_round_sticky_bits are derived from              │
│    destination_mant, which is computed from preshift_mant. Since   │
│    preshift_mant is all ones for infinity, the sticky bits become  │
│    nonzero.                                                        │
│  • Location #3: fp_regular_status.NX is computed as:               │
│     • (| fp_round_sticky_bits) OR overflow conditions              │
│       But for infinity, | fp_round_sticky_bits is already true, so │
│       NX is asserted incorrectly even when overflow should be      │
│       suppressed for infinity.                                     │
│                                                                    │
│               3. Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Preserve IEEE-754 semantics: infinity-to-float conversions      │
│    should not signal inexact unless there is a real rounding loss. │
│  • Keep the fix minimal and local to status generation logic.      │
│  • Avoid changing the mantissa/sticky-bit generation path unless   │
│    necessary, since it may be shared by other rounding cases.      │
│  • Ensure the existing overflow suppression for infinity remains   │
│    intact.                                                         │
│  • Do not alter unrelated integer conversion behavior.             │
│                                                                    │
│                     4. How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ The cleanest fix is to suppress NX for                             │
│ floating-point-to-floating-point conversions when the source is    │
│ infinity.                                                          │
│                                                                    │
│ Since the code already suppresses OF for infinity via              │
│ ~info_q.is_inf, NX should similarly ignore sticky bits when        │
│ info_q.is_inf is true in the FP destination path.                  │
│                                                                    │
│ A minimal fix is to change:                                        │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  assign fp_regular_status.NX = src_is_int_q ? (|                   │
│  fp_round_sticky_bits)                                             │
│              : (| fp_round_sticky_bits) | (~info_q.is_inf &        │
│  (of_before_round | of_after_round));                              │
