│                                                                    │
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                         1. Problem summary                         │
│                                                                    │
│ The bug is in fpnew_opgroup_multifmt_slice: when slicing operands  │
│ for each lane, it always uses the bit width of src_fmt_i for all   │
│ operands.                                                          │
│ That is correct for operands 0 and 1, but incorrect for operand 2  │
│ in the ADDMUL opgroup, because operand 2 and the result use the    │
│ dst_fmt_i format.                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ As a result, operands_i[2] is split incorrectly across lanes       │
│ whenever src_fmt_i and dst_fmt_i differ.                           │
│                                                                    │
│                    2. Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is in:                                                   │
│                                                                    │
│  • src/fpnew_opgroup_multifmt_slice.sv                             │
│                                                                    │
│ Specifically this code:                                            │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  always_comb begin : prepare_input                                 │
│    for (int unsigned i = 0; i < NUM_OPERANDS; i++) begin           │
│      local_operands[i] = operands_i[i] >>                          │
│  LANE*fpnew_pkg::fp_width(src_fmt_i);                              │
│    end                                                             │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This applies fp_width(src_fmt_i) to operand 2 as well.             │
│                                                                    │
│               3. Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Make the smallest possible fix.                                 │
│  • Preserve existing behavior for operands 0 and 1.                │
│  • Ensure the third operand uses dst_fmt_i only where              │
│    architecturally required.                                       │
│  • Avoid changing unrelated logic, especially conversion handling  │
│    and special cases.                                              │
│  • Keep the fix local to the operand slicing logic.                │
│                                                                    │
│                          4. How to fix it                          │
│                                                                    │
│ Update the operand slicing loop so that:                           │
│                                                                    │
│  • operand 0 and operand 1 continue to use fp_width(src_fmt_i)     │
│  • operand 2 uses fp_width(dst_fmt_i)                              │
│                                                                    │
│ This can be done with a conditional inside the loop based on i.    │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│                    Phase 2: FIX IMPLEMENTATION                     │
