│                                                                    │
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                       1) What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The test tb_axi_lite_regs occasionally fails for some random seeds │
│ because a background “direct load” process is updating the         │
│ register storage at the same time the AXI-Lite master performs the │
│ known-register readback check.                                     │
│                                                                    │
│ This creates a race:                                               │
│                                                                    │
│  • the test writes 64'hDEADBEEFDEADBEEF to address 0,              │
│  • then reads it back expecting the same value,                    │
│  • but the concurrent toggle_load() process can update one or more │
│    bytes of the same register before/during the readback,          │
│  • so the returned data becomes partially overwritten, e.g.        │
│    de01beef, causing the assertion failure.                        │
│                                                                    │
│                    2) Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is in test/tb_axi_lite_regs.sv, in the two concurrent    │
│ initial blocks:                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • proc_generate_axi_traffic: performs the write/read              │
│    expected-value check                                            │
│  • proc_generate_direct_load: launches toggle_load() tasks for     │
│    every register byte                                             │
│                                                                    │
│ The specific race is caused by toggle_load() starting too early    │
│ and running independently while the known-value test is still      │
│ executing.                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│               3) Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Avoid nondeterministic testbench races between stimulus         │
│    generators and scoreboard/checkers.                             │
│  • Ensure the directed “known value” check is completed before     │
│    random background load stimuli can modify the DUT state.        │
│  • Keep the fix minimal and localized to preserve intended random  │
│    coverage.                                                       │
│  • Do not change the functional behavior of the test more than     │
│    necessary.                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│                     4) How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Delay the start of the random direct-load tasks until after the    │
│ deterministic known-register write/read test and the subsequent    │
│ random master run have completed.                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ A minimal robust fix is:                                           │
│                                                                    │
│  • make proc_generate_direct_load wait for end_of_sim to become    │
│    asserted before launching toggle_load(),                        │
│  • since end_of_sim is only set to 1'b1 after the known-value      │
│    check and the master random run, the direct load traffic cannot │
│    interfere with the expected readback.                           │
│                                                                    │
│ This preserves the random load behavior while preventing the race. │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
