│                                                                    │
│                       1) What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The test tb_axi_lite_regs is failing intermittently depending on   │
│ the random seed because a background task updates the register     │
│ contents while the test is performing a read of the “known”        │
│ register value.                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ The failure shows that the read data is sometimes no longer        │
│ DEADBEEFDEADBEEF when the assertion runs, because a random direct  │
│ load has already modified part of the register bytes:              │
│                                                                    │
│  • expected: 64'hDEADBEEFDEADBEEF                                  │
│  • observed: 64'hDE01BEEF...-style mixed value                     │
│                                                                    │
│ So the test has a race between:                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • the deterministic read/compare sequence in                      │
│    proc_generate_axi_traffic                                       │
│  • the concurrent toggle_load() thread(s) started in               │
│    proc_generate_direct_load                                       │
│                                                                    │
│                    2) Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The problematic behavior is in test/tb_axi_lite_regs.sv,           │
│ specifically:                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • proc_generate_axi_traffic performs the write/read check of      │
│    address 0x0                                                     │
│  • proc_generate_direct_load launches toggle_load(j) for each      │
│    byte, which can alter reg_d/reg_load at arbitrary times         │
│  • toggle_load() uses randomized waits and updates register bytes  │
│    concurrently                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ The race manifests at the read assertion around:                   │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  assert (data == axi_data_t'(64'hDEADBEEFDEADBEEF))                │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│               3) Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Avoid concurrent background stimuli that can alter the DUT      │
│    state during a deterministic self-check unless synchronization  │
│    is explicit.                                                    │
│  • Keep “known value” tests isolated from random traffic, or       │
│    ensure the random traffic starts only after the deterministic   │
│    check is complete.                                              │
│  • Prefer deterministic setup for functional checks, then enable   │
│    random stress tests afterward.                                  │
│  • Minimize changes to testbench timing and concurrency unless     │
│    required.                                                       │
│                                                                    │
│                     4) How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ The cleanest fix is to delay the start of the random direct-load   │
│ threads until after the known register read/write test has         │
│ completed.                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│ That means:                                                        │
│                                                                    │
│  • do not launch toggle_load() immediately at time 0               │
│  • instead wait for the deterministic test section to finish, then │
│    start the random load processes                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ This preserves the random load stress testing while preventing it  │
│ from corrupting the expected value during the initial sanity       │
│ check.                                                             │
