│                                                                    │
│  • Avoid using a signal that is concurrently driven by unrelated   │
│    stimulus as the golden reference for a deterministic assertion. │
│  • Keep the test deterministic: the known readback check should    │
│    verify the value written by the test itself, not a value that   │
│    may be changed by background random stimulus.                   │
│  • Use a dedicated expected value variable for the known-register  │
│    check.                                                          │
│  • Minimize changes: keep random stimulus intact for the rest of   │
│    the test, but isolate the “known register” assertion from it.   │
