│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                       1) What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ Mentor Precision infers latches in the AXI data-width converter    │
│ modules (axi_dw_upsizer and axi_dw_downsizer) when synthesizing    │
│ certain combinational blocks.                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ The root cause is the use of automatic temporary variables like    │
│ r_data and w_data that are initialized from an existing signal and │
│ then conditionally overwritten inside loops. In some code paths,   │
│ Precision appears to treat these as incompletely assigned          │
│ combinational variables, leading to latch inference.               │
│                                                                    │
│ You also observed that:                                            │
│                                                                    │
│  • In the upsizer, the temporary should effectively start from a   │
│    known default ('0), and only selected lanes are overwritten.    │
│  • Synopsys synthesis does not infer latches, so the RTL is        │
│    functionally fine; this is a tool sensitivity issue.            │
│  • Adding an else branch removes the latch in at least one case,   │
│    which indicates the issue is the incomplete assignment pattern. │
│                                                                    │
│                    2) Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The problematic locations are the blocks that create and use these │
