│                                                                    │
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                       1) What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ Mentor Precision infers latches in the AXI data-width converters   │
│ (axi_dw_upsizer and axi_dw_downsizer) because some automatic       │
│ variables (r_data, w_data) are used as partially assigned          │
│ temporary data holders without an explicit default assignment path │
│ that the tool recognizes.                                          │
│                                                                    │
│ The intended behavior is:                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • start from the current stored data value,                       │
│  • selectively overwrite certain byte lanes,                       │
│  • then assign the result back.                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ However, Precision appears to interpret the temporary variable     │
│ updates as incomplete combinational assignment, which leads to     │
│ latch inference.                                                   │
│                                                                    │
│                    2) Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue occurs in the following code patterns:                   │
│                                                                    │
│  • src/axi_dw_upsizer.sv                                           │
│     • Read channel serialization block around the r_data temporary │
│     • Write channel serialization block around the w_data          │
│       temporary                                                    │
│  • src/axi_dw_downsizer.sv                                         │
│     • Read channel serialization block around the r_data temporary │
│     • Write channel serialization block around the w_data          │
│       temporary                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ From the provided snippets, the likely problematic locations are:  │
│                                                                    │
│  • axi_dw_upsizer.sv:                                              │
│     • read-side block:                                             │
│        • automatic slv_data_t r_data = slv_r_tran[t].data;         │
│     • write-side block:                                            │
│        • automatic mst_data_t w_data = w_req_d.w.data;             │
│  • axi_dw_downsizer.sv:                                            │
│     • read-side block:                                             │
│        • automatic slv_data_t r_data = r_req_d.r.data;             │
│     • write-side block:                                            │
│        • automatic mst_data_t w_data = mst_req.w.data;             │
│                                                                    │
│               3) Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Avoid relying on tool-specific interpretation of automatic      │
│    variable initialization when doing combinational byte-lane      │
│    steering.                                                       │
│  • Use explicit default assignments before conditional/loop-based  │
│    overwrites.                                                     │
│  • Keep the fix minimal and local: only change the                 │
│    initialization/assignment style, not the converter logic.       │
│  • Preserve functionality and synthesis behavior across tools.     │
│  • If an else path or default assignment removes ambiguity, prefer │
│    that over implicit initialization through declaration.          │
│                                                                    │
│                     4) How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ The safest fix is to make the temporary variables explicitly       │
│ initialized in a way that synthesis tools consistently understand. │
│                                                                    │
│ For the affected locations:                                        │
│                                                                    │
│  • initialize the temporary data variables with '0                 │
│  • then assign the source data into them explicitly before the     │
│    lane-steering loop                                              │
│                                                                    │
│ This keeps the intended semantics:                                 │
│                                                                    │
│  • start from a defined base value,                                │
│  • populate only selected lanes,                                   │
│  • then write back the modified word.                              │
│                                                                    │
│ This is the kind of change that should address Precision’s latch   │
│ inference without changing the hardware intent.                    │
│                                                                    │
