│                                                                    │
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                       1) What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ Mentor Precision infers latches in axi_dw_upsizer and              │
│ axi_dw_downsizer because some automatic temporary variables        │
│ (r_data / w_data) are initialized from a signal and then only      │
│ conditionally overwritten in a loop.                               │
│                                                                    │
│ In particular, these temporaries are used as “copy + selective     │
│ overwrite” buffers, but some synthesis tools do not reliably treat │
│ the initialization as a default assignment. That makes them think  │
│ the variable may retain its previous value, which is interpreted   │
│ as latch behavior.                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│                    2) Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue occurs in the following blocks:                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • src/axi_dw_upsizer.sv                                           │
│     • R-channel serialization:                                     │
│        • automatic slv_data_t r_data = slv_r_tran[t].data;         │
│     • W-channel serialization:                                     │
│        • automatic mst_data_t w_data = w_req_d.w.data;             │
│  • src/axi_dw_downsizer.sv                                         │
│     • R-channel serialization:                                     │
│        • automatic slv_data_t r_data = r_req_d.r.data;             │
│     • W-channel serialization:                                     │
│        • automatic mst_data_t w_data = mst_req.w.data;             │
│                                                                    │
│ The provided issue notes indicate that the upsizer case is         │
│ especially suspicious because the variable is meant to start at a  │
│ known default ('0 or the existing data value, depending on         │
│ context) and then be overwritten lane-by-lane.                     │
│                                                                    │
│               3) Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Avoid relying on automatic variable initialization as the sole  │
│    “default” value when synthesis tools may misinterpret it.       │
│  • Prefer explicit combinational defaults before conditional       │
│    updates.                                                        │
│  • Do not introduce unnecessary structural changes if only a small │
│    coding pattern change is required.                              │
│  • Keep the behavior identical for simulation and synthesis.       │
│  • Make the fix minimal and localized to the affected assignments. │
│                                                                    │
│                     4) How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ The safest fix is to avoid the pattern that triggers latch         │
│ inference by:                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • removing the automatic variable initialization at declaration,  │
│  • explicitly assigning a default value immediately after          │
│    declaration.                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ For the affected cases, an explicit assignment such as:            │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  automatic slv_data_t r_data;                                      │
│  r_data = '0;                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ or, where the design intends to preserve an existing value before  │
│ selective overwrite:                                               │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  automatic mst_data_t w_data;                                      │
│  w_data = mst_req.w.data;                                          │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ makes the intent unambiguous to synthesis tools.                   │
│                                                                    │
│ Given the issue description, the minimal fix should target the     │
│ code paths that are causing latch inference rather than rewriting  │
│ all similar blocks.                                                │
│                                                                    │
