│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                       1) What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ Mentor Precision infers latches in axi_dw_upsizer and              │
│ axi_dw_downsizer around temporary automatic variables named r_data │
│ and w_data.                                                        │
│                                                                    │
│ The root cause is that these temporaries are initialized from an   │
│ existing signal, then only conditionally overwritten inside a      │
│ loop. Some synthesis tools treat this pattern conservatively and   │
│ infer incomplete assignment/latch behavior, even though the        │
│ intended behavior is purely combinational “copy default, then      │
│ selectively overwrite.”                                            │
│                                                                    │
│                    2) Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue appears in these combinational sections:                 │
│                                                                    │
│  • src/axi_dw_upsizer.sv                                           │
│     • Read path, R_PASSTHROUGH, R_INCR_UPSIZE                      │
│        • automatic slv_data_t r_data = slv_r_tran[t].data;         │
│        • conditional byte updates in the loop                      │
│        • final assignment to slv_r_tran[t].data = r_data;          │
│     • Write path, W_PASSTHROUGH, W_INCR_UPSIZE                     │
│        • automatic mst_data_t w_data = w_req_d.w.data;             │
│        • conditional byte updates in the loop                      │
│        • final assignment to w_req_d.w.data = w_data;              │
│  • src/axi_dw_downsizer.sv                                         │
│     • Read path, R_PASSTHROUGH, R_INCR_DOWNSIZE,                   │
│       R_SPLIT_INCR_DOWNSIZE                                        │
│        • automatic slv_data_t r_data = r_req_d.r.data;             │
│     • Write path, W_PASSTHROUGH, W_INCR_DOWNSIZE,                  │
│       W_SPLIT_INCR_DOWNSIZE                                        │
│        • automatic mst_data_t w_data = mst_req.w.data;             │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is not that logic is missing in all cases; rather, the   │
│ synthesis tool is unhappy with the “initialize from current value, │
│ then partially overwrite” pattern.                                 │
│                                                                    │
│                    3) Best practices to follow                     │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep combinational logic explicitly combinational and fully     │
│    deterministic for synthesis tools.                              │
│  • Avoid relying on an automatic variable’s initialization as the  │
│    only default assignment when the variable is conditionally      │
│    modified.                                                       │
│  • Prefer an explicit default value assignment, then overwrite     │
│    only selected bits.                                             │
│  • If a signal should remain unchanged unless specific bits are    │
│    updated, initialize the temporary to '0 and then assign the     │
│    full result back from the temporary after the conditional       │
│    updates.                                                        │
│  • Make minimal changes so behavior remains unchanged for          │
│    simulators and other synthesizers.                              │
│                                                                    │
│                          4) How to fix it                          │
