│                                                                    │
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                       1) What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ axi_pkg::burst_t was changed from a fixed-width typedef (logic     │
│ [1:0]) to a width that depends on BurstWidth, which is derived     │
│ from a package parameter using $size(...).                         │
│                                                                    │
│ Vivado IP packager requires top-level HDL ports to be directly     │
│ describable from the HDL file, and it does not handle this kind of │
│ package-dependent typedef in IP port declarations well. As a       │
│ result, custom Vivado IPs using axi_pkg::burst_t at their top      │
│ level fail packaging.                                              │
│                                                                    │
│                    2) Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The relevant problematic location is:                              │
│                                                                    │
│  • src/axi_pkg.sv                                                  │
│     • burst_t typedef at the top of the package                    │
│     • BurstWidth parameter derived from $size(burst_t)             │
│     • any code using BurstWidth in width computations is           │
│       indirectly tied to the same issue                            │
│                                                                    │
│ From the provided locations, the core issue is specifically:       │
│                                                                    │
│  • typedef logic [1:0] burst_t;                                    │
│  • parameter int unsigned BurstWidth = $size(burst_t);             │
│                                                                    │
│ The downstream width functions (aw_width, ar_width) use            │
│ BurstWidth, but they are not the root cause. The root cause is the │
│ typedef/parameter coupling that makes the type less friendly to    │
│ Vivado packaging.                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│               3) Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep top-level HDL port types simple and statically obvious to  │
│    IP packagers.                                                   │
│  • Avoid deriving package-visible type widths from $size(...) of   │
│    typedefs when those typedefs are used in module port            │
│    declarations.                                                   │
│  • Prefer a pattern where:                                         │
│     • the numeric width is defined first as a plain                │
│       constant/parameter,                                          │
│     • the typedef is derived from that numeric width.              │
│  • Make minimal changes to preserve existing behavior and avoid    │
│    rippling interface changes through the codebase.                │
│                                                                    │
│                     4) How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ The best fix is to invert the dependency:                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • define BurstWidth as a numeric constant directly, e.g. 2        │
│  • define burst_t using BurstWidth, e.g. typedef logic             │
│    [BurstWidth-1:0] burst_t;                                       │
│                                                                    │
│ This keeps the externally used type stable and makes the width     │
│ explicit, which is more compatible with Vivado IP packaging.       │
│                                                                    │
│ No other changes are necessary in the shown code unless there are  │
│ separate usages that still depend on the old direction of the      │
│ dependency.                                                        │
