│                                                                    │
│                       1) What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ axi_pkg::burst_t was changed from a plain fixed-width typedef to a │
│ width that depends on the Verilog parameter BurstWidth via         │
│ $size(burst_t).                                                    │
│ This breaks Vivado IP packaging because Vivado requires top-level  │
│ IP port types to be directly describable in the HDL file’s port    │
│ declaration, and it does not handle package typedefs that depend   │
│ on package parameters in this context.                             │
│                                                                    │
│ In short: using axi_pkg::burst_t as part of a top-level packaged   │
│ IP interface is no longer Vivado-compatible.                       │
│                                                                    │
│                    2) Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is rooted in src/axi_pkg.sv:                             │
│                                                                    │
│  • burst_t is defined as a typedef.                                │
│  • BurstWidth is then derived from $size(burst_t).                 │
│  • aw_width() and ar_width() use BurstWidth in width calculations. │
│                                                                    │
│ Relevant locations from the provided code:                         │
│                                                                    │
│  • Location #1:                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│     typedef logic [1:0]  burst_t;                                  │
│     parameter int unsigned BurstWidth  = $size(burst_t);           │
│                                                                    │
│  • Locations #2 and #4:                                            │
│    BurstWidth is used in aw_width() and ar_width().                │
│                                                                    │
│               3) Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep package-level constants self-contained and tool-friendly.  │
│  • Avoid making top-level interface typing depend on               │
│    package-internal $size() expressions when targeting Vivado IP   │
│    packaging.                                                      │
│  • Prefer explicit numeric parameters for widths when they are     │
│    part of interface definitions.                                  │
│  • Preserve backward compatibility and minimize code changes.      │
│  • Ensure width constants remain consistent with their associated  │
│    typedefs.                                                       │
│                                                                    │
│                     4) How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ The best fix is to define the width first as a plain numeric       │
│ parameter, then define the typedef from that parameter.            │
│                                                                    │
│ That means changing:                                               │
│                                                                    │
│  • burst_t should be declared using BurstWidth                     │
│  • BurstWidth should be a fixed numeric constant, not derived from │
│    $size(burst_t)                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ This removes the dependency cycle and makes the package more       │
│ Vivado-friendly.                                                   │
│                                                                    │
