│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  parameter int unsigned BurstWidth = $size(burst_t);               │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Vivado IP packager does not like top-level IP port types that      │
│ depend on package-local typedefs/parameters in a way that is not   │
│ directly visible in the HDL port description. Because of that,     │
│ using axi_pkg::burst_t in a custom packaged Vivado IP top can fail │
│ packaging, even though the code is otherwise valid SystemVerilog.  │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is not with AXI semantics; it is a Vivado compatibility  │
│ problem caused by how the width is derived.                        │
│                                                                    │
│                    2) Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The problematic code is in src/axi_pkg.sv, specifically:           │
│                                                                    │
│  • burst_t typedef declaration                                     │
│  • BurstWidth parameter definition                                 │
│  • downstream uses of BurstWidth in aw_width() and ar_width()      │
│                                                                    │
│ Relevant locations from the provided snippets:                     │
│                                                                    │
│  • Location #1: typedef logic [1:0] burst_t; and parameter int     │
│    unsigned BurstWidth = $size(burst_t);                           │
│  • Location #2: aw_width() uses BurstWidth                         │
│  • Location #4 / #5: ar_width() uses BurstWidth                    │
│                                                                    │
│               3) Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep the fix minimal and avoid changing unrelated API behavior. │
│  • Preserve the intended bit width of AXI burst fields (2 bits)    │
│    without relying on a package typedef for size inference.        │
│  • Prefer explicit numeric constants for widths when tool          │
│    compatibility is an issue, especially for vendor IP packagers.  │
│  • Ensure existing functions still compute the same widths so      │
│    downstream code remains unaffected.                             │
│  • Avoid introducing broader refactors unless necessary.           │
│                                                                    │
│                     4) How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Make BurstWidth independent of the burst_t typedef by assigning it │
│ an explicit numeric value, e.g. 32'd2, instead of $size(burst_t).  │
│                                                                    │
│ This preserves the same functionality while avoiding the Vivado    │
│ packaging issue. No other logic changes are required, since        │
│ aw_width() and ar_width() already consume BurstWidth and will      │
│ continue to evaluate correctly.                                    │
