╭─ Patch Generation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                    │
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                       1. What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ axi_pkg::burst_t was changed from a plain typedef with a fixed     │
│ bit-width to a typedef whose width is tied to a package parameter  │
│ (BurstWidth = $size(burst_t)).                                     │
│                                                                    │
│ Vivado IP packager does not like package-based type/parameter      │
│ dependencies for top-level IP ports unless the HDL file explicitly │
│ contains the port descriptions in a form Vivado can resolve. As a  │
│ result, custom Vivado IPs that expose axi_pkg::burst_t-based       │
│ structures at their top level can no longer be packaged correctly. │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is not with the functional AXI logic itself, but with    │
│ how type widths are defined and derived for Vivado compatibility.  │
│                                                                    │
│                    2. Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The relevant code is in src/axi_pkg.sv, specifically:              │
│                                                                    │
│  • burst_t definition                                              │
│  • BurstWidth parameter definition                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The root cause is this dependency chain:                           │
│                                                                    │
│  • burst_t is defined as a typedef                                 │
│  • BurstWidth is derived from $size(burst_t)                       │
│  • then other functions use BurstWidth in width computations       │
│                                                                    │
│ The problematic lines are in Location #1, and the downstream       │
│ consumers are the width functions in Locations #2, #4, #5.         │
│                                                                    │
│               3. Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep package constants and typedef widths independent of        │
│    parameter evaluation when possible.                             │
│  • Prefer explicit numeric width parameters for tool               │
│    compatibility, especially with vendor IP packagers.             │
│  • Preserve backward compatibility for the rest of the AXI package │
│    API.                                                            │
│  • Make the smallest possible change to fix Vivado packaging       │
│    without changing the semantics of the AXI types.                │
│                                                                    │
│                     4. How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ The best fix is to define the typedef width numerically first, and │
│ then define the type using that parameter, rather than deriving    │
│ the parameter from $size(typedef).                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In practice:                                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • change burst_t to use a numeric width directly (logic           │
│    [BurstWidth-1:0])                                               │
│  • set BurstWidth to the literal value 32'd2                       │
│  • optionally use the same style for other widths if needed, but   │
│    the reported issue is specifically about burst_t / BurstWidth   │
│                                                                    │
│ This removes the circular/tool-unfriendly dependency and makes     │
│ Vivado IP packager able to resolve the port types.                 │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│                    Phase 2: FIX IMPLEMENTATION                     │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  [file]src/axi_pkg.sv[/file]                                       │
│  [original]                                                        │
