│                                                                    │
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                       1) What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The axi_riscv_lrsc module computes the number of reservation-clear │
│ operations for AXI write bursts incorrectly.                       │
│                                                                    │
│ For an AW burst of length N, it currently clears/checks N+1        │
│ addresses instead of the correct N addresses in the range:         │
│                                                                    │
│  • current behavior: [A, A + N]                                    │
│  • correct behavior: [A, A + (N - 1)]                              │
│                                                                    │
│ So the burst handling over-clears by one address.                  │
│                                                                    │
│                    2) Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The bug is in src/axi_riscv_lrsc.sv, in the AW-channel handling    │
│ logic where the code initializes clr_len_d for burst writes.       │
│                                                                    │
│ The relevant logic is in the AW_IDLE branch, around the section:   │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  if (aw_res_len > 1) begin                                         │
│      clr_addr_d = slv_aw_addr_i[AXI_ADDR_WIDTH-1:AXI_ADDR_LSB] +   │
│      clr_len_d  = aw_res_len - 1;                                  │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ and then in AW_BURST the module repeatedly clears addresses until  │
│ clr_len_q reaches zero.                                            │
│                                                                    │
│ Because clr_len_d is set to aw_res_len - 1, and the starting       │
│ address is already included in the first clear request, the module │
│ ends up clearing one extra address.                                │
│                                                                    │
│               3) Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep the fix minimal and localized.                             │
│  • Preserve the existing AW burst state-machine behavior.          │
│  • Ensure the number of generated clear requests exactly matches   │
│    the intended burst address span.                                │
│  • Avoid changing unrelated logic or interfaces.                   │
│  • Maintain the current semantics for non-burst and single-beat    │
│    transactions.                                                   │
│                                                                    │
│                     4) How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Adjust the initial clear-length calculation so the burst clear     │
│ loop iterates over exactly the remaining addresses after the first │
│ one.                                                               │
│                                                                    │
│ Since the first address is handled immediately, the remaining      │
│ number of addresses is aw_res_len - 2, not aw_res_len - 1.         │
│                                                                    │
│ So change:                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  clr_len_d  = aw_res_len - 1;                                      │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ to:                                                                │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  clr_len_d  = aw_res_len - 2;                                      │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This ensures a burst of length N clears exactly N addresses total. │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
