First, the root of the bug lives in the integer clock‐divider’s FSM where a divide-by-0 value never lets you exit the WAIT_END_PERIOD state – so “src/clk_int_div.sv” must be fixed.  Downstream of that change you’ll also need to update or add any package definitions, documentation, and the functional testbench to either guard against or verify the new 0-divide behavior.  In this repo that maps to:

```text
src/clk_int_div.sv
src/clk_int_div_pkg.sv
src/clk_int_div_tb.sv
README.md
