│ The clock divider gets stuck when the divider value is programmed  │
│ to 0.                                                              │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is triggered when valid_i is tied high and div_i can     │
│ take the reset value 0. After loading div_q = 0, the divider can   │
│ no longer complete its reconfiguration sequence, because it waits  │
│ for a condition that can never become true.                        │
│                                                                    │
│                    2) Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The problematic logic is in src/clk_int_div.sv, inside the         │
│ WAIT_END_PERIOD state:                                             │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  if (cycle_cntr_q == div_q - 1) begin                              │
│    clk_gate_state_d = IDLE;                                        │
│  end                                                               │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ When div_q == 0, the expression div_q - 1 underflows, so the       │
│ comparison becomes invalid for the intended behavior. This means   │
│ the FSM can remain stuck in WAIT_END_PERIOD.                       │
│                                                                    │
│               3) Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Handle special divider values explicitly, especially bypass     │
│    modes such as div == 0 and div == 1.                            │
│  • Avoid relying on arithmetic underflow/overflow in state         │
│    transition conditions.                                          │
│  • Keep the fix minimal and localized to the FSM transition logic. │
│  • Preserve the existing intended behavior for all other divider   │
│    values.                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│                     4) How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Update the WAIT_END_PERIOD transition condition so that bypass     │
│ values do not require waiting for a cycle-counter match that       │
│ cannot happen.                                                     │
│                                                                    │
│ A minimal and correct fix is:                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • allow immediate transition back to IDLE when                    │
│    clk_div_bypass_en_q is asserted, or                             │
│  • equivalently, guard the div_q - 1 comparison so it is only used │
│    for non-bypass divider values.                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ This keeps the divider reconfigurable when div_i = 0, while        │
│ preserving normal behavior for non-bypass configurations.          │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│                    Phase 2: FIX IMPLEMENTATION                     │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  [file]src/clk_int_div.sv[/file]                                   │
│  [original]                                                        │
│        WAIT_END_PERIOD: begin                                      │
│          gate_en_d     = 1'b0;                                     │
│          // Keep the toggle flip-flops disabled until we reach id  │
│  state.                                                            │
│          // Otherwise, the start state of the t-ffs depends on th  │
│  number of wait                                                    │
│          // cycles which would yield different output clock phase  │
│  depending on                                                      │
│          // the number of wait cycles.                             │
│          toggle_ffs_en = 1'b0;                                     │
│          if (cycle_cntr_q == div_q - 1) begin                      │
│            clk_gate_state_d = IDLE;                                │
│          end                                                       │
