│                                                                    │
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                       1) What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The clock divider gets stuck after programming a divider value of  │
│ 0.                                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The reported behavior is:                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • valid_i is tied high                                            │
│  • div_i is driven by a register that resets to 0                  │
│  • once div_q == 0 is loaded, the divider can no longer be         │
│    reconfigured                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ The root cause is that the state machine enters WAIT_END_PERIOD,   │
│ but its exit condition compares:                                   │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  if (cycle_cntr_q == div_q - 1)                                    │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ When div_q == 0, this becomes cycle_cntr_q == -1, which is not a   │
│ reachable condition for the unsigned cycle counter. As a result,   │
│ the FSM never leaves WAIT_END_PERIOD.                              │
│                                                                    │
│                    2) Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is in src/clk_int_div.sv, in the WAIT_END_PERIOD state:  │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  WAIT_END_PERIOD: begin                                            │
│    gate_en_d     = 1'b0;                                           │
│    toggle_ffs_en = 1'b0;                                           │
│    if (cycle_cntr_q == div_q - 1) begin                            │
│      clk_gate_state_d = IDLE;                                      │
│    end                                                             │
│  end                                                               │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This logic fails for divider values 0 and also conceptually relies │
│ on a countdown-style comparison that does not work for the bypass  │
│ case.                                                              │
│                                                                    │
│               3) Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep the fix minimal and localized.                             │
│  • Preserve the intended FSM behavior for all valid divider        │
│    values.                                                         │
│  • Treat divider 0 consistently with the existing bypass behavior  │
│    (div == 0 or div == 1).                                         │
│  • Avoid introducing changes to unrelated logic unless necessary.  │
│  • Ensure the FSM can always return to IDLE after loading a bypass │
│    divider, so reconfiguration remains possible.                   │
